.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/postcss-selector-parser Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "postcss-selector-parser [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/postcss/postcss-selector-parser.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/postcss/postcss-selector-parser)"
.PP
.RS 4
Selector parser with built in methods for working with selector strings\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
With \fRnpm\fP do:

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install postcss\-selector\-parser
.fi
.PP
.SH "Quick Start"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const parser = require('postcss\-selector\-parser');
const transform = selectors => {
    selectors\&.walk(selector => {
        // do something with the selector
        console\&.log(String(selector))
    });
};

const transformed = parser(transform)\&.processSync('h1, h2, h3');
.fi
.PP

.PP
To normalize selector whitespace:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const parser = require('postcss\-selector\-parser');
const normalized = parser()\&.processSync('h1, h2, h3', {lossless: false});
// \-> h1,h2,h3
.fi
.PP

.PP
Async support is provided through \fRparser\&.process\fP and will resolve a Promise with the resulting selector string\&.
.SH "API"
.PP
Please see \fBAPI\&.md\fP\&.
